From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: agent <agent@local>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] vayu_sms: fix WMS wire requests (List mode, Raw Send TPDU),
 dump request/reply

List Messages omitted the GW message mode TLV; this modem answered result 1
error 17.  libqmi's qmi-errors.h says 17 is MISSING_ARGUMENT, not encoding, so
the fix is the mode TLV 0x12 = 1 (libqmi qmi-service-wms.json: tag 0x11, mode
0x12).  Delete gets the same mode TLV.

Raw Send now sends the SMS-SUBMIT TPDU alone, without the leading 0x00 SMSC
prefix (the modem takes the SMSC from EF_SMSC, as Android's RIL does), and sets
SMS-on-IMS TLV 0x13 = 0.  vayu_sms_smsc=1 restores the old full-PDU form.  Its
reply wait is 30 s: the 142105 run had a weak LTE signal.

The first 48 bytes of the List and Raw Send requests are printed in hex with the
destination BCD bytes shown as "xx"; the raw reply is printed as result/error,
its TLV list and the CDMA/GSM cause TLVs.  qmi_txn gained an optional raw copy
of the reply for this, and Get Supported Messages (0x001E) is logged at start.
